# vendored engine sources + vendored upstream DSH runtime packages — pinned
# + sha256-verified by runtime/spike/vendor/ensure.sh and ensure-dsh.sh;
# untracked so the syntax-class checker never judges upstream C or the
# verbatim upstream JS bundles (adaptation lives in our shims, never in the
# vendored copies — D6/D9; the pin tables in the ensure scripts are the
# tracked provenance record)
runtime/spike/vendor/quickjs-ng/
runtime/spike/vendor/dsh/
runtime/spike/vendor/npm/
# The WebAssembly interpreter (wasm3) is vendored on the same terms — pinned +
# sha256-verified by runtime/spike/vendor/ensure-wasm3.sh, untracked for the
# same reason as the engines above: upstream's real-world C cannot survive an
# editor-level parse gate, and the pin table is the provenance record.
runtime/spike/vendor/wasm3/

# The emulated-Linux userland engine (iSH-arm64) is vendored on exactly those
# terms — pinned + sha256-verified by runtime/spike/vendor/ensure-ish.sh, kept
# VERBATIM (D6: adaptation lives in our own host layer, never in the engine), and
# untracked so the content gates never judge ~1,000 files of upstream C/asm that
# no editor-level parse gate can survive. The pin table in the ensure script is
# the tracked provenance record; the fork's GPL text travels with the sources.
runtime/spike/vendor/ish/
# …and the guest USERLAND that app rides in the iOS bundle: the pinned Alpine
# minirootfs, fetched + sha256-verified by
# runtime/spike/vendor/ensure-ish-rootfs.sh, which is the tracked provenance
# record. Untracked for the usual two reasons — a 3.8 MB binary in git, and the
# content gates have no business parsing a tarball.
hosts/ios/App/Generated/ish-rootfs.tar.gz

# The Android asset stage of the D9 spine closure is the SAME vendored
# upstream code, untracked for the same reason (the stage script is the
# reproducible materializer; the web-boot closure below stayed tracked at
# #63 and is frozen as-is):
#   hosts/android/ci/stage-spine-closure.sh — byte-identity-verified copy
#   from the ensure-dsh.sh pin, wired into the Gradle build (stageSpineClosure)
hosts/android/app/src/main/assets/spike/vendor/dsh/agent@*/
hosts/android/app/src/main/assets/spike/vendor/dsh/agent-loop@*/
hosts/android/app/src/main/assets/spike/vendor/dsh/brand@*/
hosts/android/app/src/main/assets/spike/vendor/dsh/llm@*/
hosts/android/app/src/main/assets/spike/vendor/dsh/sandbox@*/
hosts/android/app/src/main/assets/spike/vendor/dsh/scope@*/
hosts/android/app/src/main/assets/spike/vendor/dsh/session@*/
hosts/android/app/src/main/assets/spike/vendor/dsh/session-projection@*/
hosts/android/app/src/main/assets/spike/vendor/dsh/settings@*/
hosts/android/app/src/main/assets/spike/vendor/dsh/system-prompt@*/
hosts/android/app/src/main/assets/spike/vendor/dsh/timeout@*/
hosts/android/app/src/main/assets/spike/vendor/dsh/tools@*/
hosts/android/app/src/main/assets/spike/vendor/dsh/typert-protocol@*/
hosts/android/app/src/main/assets/spike/vendor/dsh/util-values@*/
hosts/android/app/src/main/assets/spike/vendor/npm/zod@*/

# Python
__pycache__/
.gov/tasks/.new.lock
# `gov decision add` takes this lock and by design NEVER unlinks it (the
# close-and-unlink form is a classic lockfile race — gov/decision.py:_locked
# keeps the path stable so a second writer cannot slip into a fresh inode).
# The sibling .gov/tasks/.new.lock above is ignored for the same reason; this
# one lands under docs/, so without this line it is permanent `git status`
# noise in an otherwise clean tree.
docs/.decision.lock
runtime/spike/logs-upstream.txt
runtime/spike/logs-upstream-boot.txt
runtime/spike/logs-settings-surfaces.txt

# D9 W-HARMONY3: the pinned zod classic closure inside the harmony rawfile
# spine closure. VERBATIM upstream bytes (sha256-pinned by
# runtime/spike/vendor/ensure-dsh.sh, copied + cmp-verified by
# hosts/harmony/ci/vendor-official.sh) that the syntax-class checker cannot
# parse (`export { _instanceof as instanceof }` — a tree-sitter-javascript
# false positive on valid ES module syntax), and upstream discipline (D6)
# forbids editing the bytes to satisfy a checker. Untracked for the same
# reason as officialweb/ above: the content gates never judge vendored
# upstream JS; the vendor script is the materialize + verify step.
hosts/harmony/entry/src/main/resources/rawfile/spike/vendor/npm/zod@4.4.3/

# graphify knowledge-graph analysis output (local tooling artifact, not product)
graphify-out/
